From 78601a1d2996788d1036b09a55e62784e523d89b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suiyan <suiyan@sunmmio.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 15:42:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dadao: real fork/context switch
 (copy_thread/__switch_to/ret_from_fork) (KL-156a)

kernel_thread() previously always failed (-ENOSYS) because
arch/dadao/kernel/process.c had no real copy_thread()/__switch_to();
kernel_init (and kthreadd, kworkers, every later kernel thread) was
never actually created or executed. This implements the real fork and
context-switch plumbing:

- switch.S (new): dadao_switch_to_asm() saves/restores the frozen
  KL-140a cooperative frame (rb1..rb4, rd32..rd63, rb32..rb63, full
  ra0..ra63 via the ldmo-ra/stmo-ra contract) between kernel stacks,
  with its final ret popping the NEXT task's RegRAS; dadao_ret_from_fork
  is the fresh-task entry (schedule_tail(prev), fn(arg), do_exit(0)).
- process.c: __switch_to() is a C wrapper (WRITE_ONCE current, mask
  global CFX delivery across the switch, call the asm helper, return
  prev); copy_thread() builds the fake switch frame for kernel threads
  (fn/arg ride in frame words w0/w1, ra63 points at ret_from_fork).
- asm-offsets.c: THREAD_KERNEL_SP_OFFSET for switch.S.
- init/main.c + dadao-m1.h: CONFIG_DADAO_M1_PROGRESS markers observing
  the idle->kernel_init round trip (SWITCH_FROM_IDLE/SWITCH_TO_IDLE),
  a diagnostic yield that lets the scheduler genuinely run the boot/idle
  task again, and how-far markers (ROOT_MOUNT_ATTEMPT/EXEC_INIT_ATTEMPT).

Real bug found and fixed while bringing this up: the switch frame
(0x438) lives at [SP-0x438, SP) on the current kernel stack, exactly
inside the window entry.S's real trap frame (0x640) carves out on every
TIMER dispatch -- a timer firing during the switch's save could silently
corrupt the outgoing task's saved context. The switch is therefore a
masked critical section (local_irq_save/restore); a pending TIMER stays
latched and delivers immediately after the unmask.

Boot now reaches kernel_init and the real scheduler: 1000+ genuine
context switches, kthreadd/workqueue machinery running, then the next
honest wall (VFS root mount panic, no userspace on the dadao-m1 machine).
